# THE OFFSETS ARE UTF-8 BYTES into guests/rust/ranges.rs's document,
# whose first line is CJK — so every match sits SIX BYTES further along
# than in UTF-16, the unit four of the five backends count. Each
# assertion carries the COVERED TEXT too, since the core converts into
# the backend's unit and back and two symmetric mistakes cancel. THIS
# FILE IS PURE ASCII (docs/ranges-units.md §8.7).
expect label#0 "0 matches"
# NOTHING IS DECORATED YET: a backend that decorated everything, or
# answered from a stale read, fails here before the next line.
expect_highlights textarea#0 ""
click button#0
expect label#0 "3 matches"
expect_highlights textarea#0 "57:62=alpha|203:208=alpha|753:758=alpha"
expect_selection textarea#0 "203:208=alpha"
# The `offscreen` leg is what makes the `visible` one mean something: on
# a document short enough to fit, containment is true before anything
# scrolls and the verb passes vacuously.
expect_revealed textarea#0 753:758 offscreen
click button#1
expect_revealed textarea#0 753:758 visible
# A REVEAL IS A PURE EFFECT: the declared set and the selection are
# unmoved.
expect_highlights textarea#0 "57:62=alpha|203:208=alpha|753:758=alpha"
expect_selection textarea#0 "203:208=alpha"
# D2 — A TEXT EDIT DROPS THE DECLARED SET, never shifts it: kaya tracks
# nothing across an edit and the app re-declares from text_changed.
# `type` goes in through the platform's own input path, so this is a
# user's keystroke and not a write kaya made.
click button#2
expect_focused textarea#0
type " z"
expect label#0 "0 matches"
expect_highlights textarea#0 ""
# D4 — A SELECTION ARRIVING MID-COMPOSITION IS REFUSED: honouring it
# would COMMIT the marked text mid-word and shift every later offset.
# THE OBSERVABLE IS THE CARET, parked at the end of the marked text —
# had the select been honoured this would read `57:62=alpha`.
compose textarea#0 "nihon"
click button#3
expect_selection textarea#0 "820:820="
